t burn scars will also be especially susceptible and these\ninclude the Lee and Elk RX, Gold Mountain and Elk, Ferris, and\nBabylon burn scars to name a few.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Central Yampa River Basin; Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley; Debeque to Silt Corridor; Central Colorado River Basin; Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; Central Gunnison and Uncompahgre River Basin; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops; Upper Gunnison River Valley; Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Southeast Utah; Tavaputs Plateau; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 30 at 11:36AM MDT until September 1 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin and San Juan River Basin.\n\n* WHEN...From Monday morning through Monday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nRecent burn scars will also be especially susceptible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Monsoonal moisture will remain across the area through Monday\nevening and will support thunderstorms and showers with heavy\nrainfall across the watch area. Several rounds of heavier rain\nare expected increasing the chance for flash flooding especially\nin our more susceptible areas.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf53ca765d0cc18c1b080bdda7ac3b081a211a37.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T17:51:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 301751 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1151 AM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Multiple rounds of showers and storms are expected today, especially along and north of I-70. - Another wet day is on tap tomorrow as well, with higher coverage of precipitation across southeast Utah and southwest Colorado. - Flash flooding is possible th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-30T07:39:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Showers and thunderstorms will continue each afternoon through the next several days. Heavy rain, gust outflow winds and ligthning will be the biggest concerns. Temperatures will also drop thanks to increased cloud cover and precipitation. Fire weather concerns remain minimal. A downturn in precip is possible on Tuesday. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THU","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KAEJ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KAEJ 301755Z AUTO 07005KT 10SM SCT065 SCT085 BKN100 21/05 A3032 RMK AO2 T02130048 10213 20105","temp_f":70,"wind_dir":70,"wind_kt":5,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":